= Using the signal classes =

Signals allow one processes to interrupt the execution of another process.

Signal handlers allow processes to intercept and react to the signals sent to them.

Rudiments provides 3 classes for working with signals: [../classes/html/classsignalset.html signalset], [../classes/html/classsignalmanager.html signalmanager] and [../classes/html/classsignalhandler.html signalhandler].

A signal set is just a collection of signals.  The [../classes/html/classsignalset.html signalset class] allows a programmer to build up a collection of signals.

The [../classes/html/classsignalmanager.html signalmanager class] provides methods for sending signals, ignoring signals, waiting for signals and examining blocked signals.

The [../classes/html/classsignalhandler.html signalhandler class] provides methods for catching and handling signals.

This program illustrates the use of all three classes.

